--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/4 key facts kept) ---
I was depressed by the black New Year, by the strike in South Wales, and by the hope that the trouble would be patched up.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
Friday, January 2, 1931. To-day I have resolved never again to make an entry in the books of the office, until I have thoroughly assured myself of its correctness.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
Friday opened gloomily, with more than two and a half million out of work; the coal and cotton trades are in dispute, and a general strike in South Wales has thrown 150,000 miners out of work. I hope the Conciliation Board will arrange a temporary settlement, so that the men may return to work.
