--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/1 key facts kept) ---
1. Read in The Times that there was little activity in the great South Wales collieries, where last night negotiations between miners, operators and government officials ended in a sort of combined strike and lockout.
   ☾ Ada (forgotten by morning): She dreamt that she and Fred walked together hand in hand down a pleasant country lane, and came to a stile.  He helped her over, and they kissed each other good-night.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that Mr. Thomas raised his salary to £4 a week.

