--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (2/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I had 13s. 4d. in my pocket, and owed 7s. for rent.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (0/3 key facts kept) ---
I resolve never to make an entry in the books of my office, until I am thoroughly satisfied of its correctness; and I read in the paper that the New Year opens gloomily, and that more than two and a half million are out of work, and the coal and cotton trades are in a bad way.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I set Mr. Hale to balance the quarterly ledger.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that she was dead, and that Bert and she were carried to the cemetery, and buried in one grave.
   ☾ Arthur: He dreamt that he was promoted to be chief clerk at a salary of £500 a year.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was walking up and down outside the office, watching to see that it was properly cleaned.

